· To be eligible to register to vote, a person must: be a U.S. Citizen and current resident of Kentucky not less than 28 days before the election;

o be at least 18 years old by the date of the next general election;

o not be a convicted felon (or, if convicted of a felony, my right to vote has been restored following an expungement, Executive Pardon, or Executive Order;

o not have been judged mentally incompetent in a court of law and have voting rights removed;

o not claim the right to vote anywhere outside Kentucky;

o See Kentucky Constitution § 145

· See KRS 116.055 (https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/law/statutes/statute.aspx?id=48900).
